.env
.env.local
# Any .env sidecar — backups, dated copies, .env.bak-<date>, .env.old.
# Added 2026-09-08 after a pre-edit backup named `.env.bak-2026-09-08` landed
# untracked-but-committable in this PUBLIC repo, holding an exposed Proxmox
# token, a hypervisor password and an API key. `.env` alone did not cover it.
# The negation keeps a committed template possible if one is ever added here.
.env.*
!.env.example
node_modules/

# Machine-local stream-coordination registry (see CLAUDE.md's "Parallel
# work" section) — only created if a project adopts that pattern.
ACTIVE.md

# --- df-overseer ---

# Infrastructure specifics (Proxmox host, Coolify, IPs, hostnames, tokens).
# Committed counterparts live alongside as infra/local.example.*
infra/local.*
# ...but the example counterparts ARE meant to be committed (CLAUDE.md).
# Without this negation the pattern above swallows them and a fresh
# clone gets no template to fill in at all.
!infra/local.example.*

# DF saves — 15-19 MB each, git handles them badly. Worldgen params ARE
# tracked (see worlds/) so a world can be reproduced without the save.
save/
*.dfsave
# Save archives pulled off the VM by scripts/install_df.py backup.
backups/

# Ingested wiki corpus — large, regenerable from the WikiTeam dump process
# documented in docs/MEMORY.md. Do not commit.
corpus/
*.xml.gz

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.venv_perception/

# Machine-local Claude Code scheduled-task lock.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Terraform / OpenTofu, added 2026-09-08 ahead of any `terraform init`.
# State files hold resource attributes in cleartext and are the same class of
# near-miss as the .env sidecar above: untracked is not the same as safe in a
# repo where an agent may run `git add -A`. The negation keeps a committed
# example tfvars possible.
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform/
.terraform.lock.hcl
*.tfvars
!*.tfvars.example
.venv-dfmcp/

# dfqueue's live SQLite database(s) -- real fort data, one per fort, default
# dfqueue/<fort>.sqlite3 (handoffs/2026-09-15-live-signals-sqlite.md). WAL
# mode also leaves -wal/-shm sidecar files alongside it.
dfqueue/*.sqlite3*
# production/<fort>.sqlite3, same pattern (handoffs/2026-09-18-production-package.md).
production/*.sqlite3*
# dfseries/<fort>.series.sqlite3, same pattern again (handoffs/2026-09-19-dfseries-store.md).
dfseries/*.sqlite3*

# The conductor's own runtime archive (handoffs/2026-09-22-loop-conductor-
# service.md; docs/AGENT-LOOP.md item 3): each cycle's briefing, every role
# run's JSON envelope, cost and clock changes, plus per-role diff cursors
# and the daily cost log -- all real, per-fort operational data written by
# the running service on VM 106, never source. See conductor/archive.py and
# conductor/cursors.py.
runtime/
